// =============================================================================
// Motorcycle K7 Auto-Power — Shelly Plus Uni (garage) + Omron G6S-2 (machine)
// =============================================================================
// REBUILT 2026-09-12. The Shelly moved off the motorcycle and into the garage.
// Anything you remember about a MOSFET on the bike is gone — see the block at
// the end of this header for what it looked like.
//
// What is switched: the K7's YELLOW wire, an ignition SENSE input. The camera's
// RED wire is permanent 12 V straight from the battery and is never switched.
// Nothing in this project has ever switched the camera's power.
//
// Flow: Charger detected AND garage lead connected -> Shelly relay closes ->
//       G6S-2 coil energises -> its contact drives K7 YELLOW -> camera wakes ->
//       Pi dumps footage -> Dump complete -> relay opens -> camera sleeps.
//
// Physical wiring:
//   GARAGE    - Shelly on mains; 12 V PSU
//             - PSU(+) -> relay COM;  relay NO -> lead core 1
//             - lead core 2 -> 100 ohm -> PSU(-)
//             - Shelly ADC (Voltmeter:100) taps the COIL SIDE of the 100 ohm
//   LEAD      - 2 x 0.5 mm2, cores numbered 1 and 2, Deutsch DTM 2-way
//   MACHINE   - G6S-2 DPDT, 1 kOhm 12 V coil. DTM 1 -> coil + (relay pin 12),
//               DTM 2 -> coil - (relay pin 1)
//             - contact pin 9 (COM) <- battery +12 V fused; pin 8 (NO) -> K7
//               YELLOW, via the existing 1N4007 from the ignition circuit
//
// The ADC no longer measures a battery. It measures coil current:
//   lead connected, coil energised   0.850 - 0.880 V
//   lead unplugged, or coil open     0.000 V
// Battery voltage now comes from Vehicle10_Power (the FMM920 tracker), which
// agreed with the old ADC reading to 4 mV when both were live on 2026-09-08.
//
// The 0.27 V ADC offset is NOT applied any more. It was a battery-voltage
// calibration; against a 0.86 V coil signal it has no meaning. It survives only
// as the reason the ADC's noise floor clamps anything under 0.27 V to zero.
//
// The lead cannot be sensed passively — the resistor only carries current when
// the coil is energised, so an open relay reads 0.000 V whether the lead is in
// or out. See vehicle-motorcycle-k7-lead.js, which probes instead of polling.
//
// WHAT THIS REPLACED (until 2026-09-12)
//   The Shelly sat on the motorcycle, fed from its battery, drawing 80-110 mA
//   around the clock. Its relay pulled an IRFP9140N P-channel MOSFET gate to
//   ground through 100 ohm, against a 10K pull-up that held the MOSFET off
//   whenever the Shelly was unpowered. The MOSFET drain drove K7 YELLOW.
//   Its ADC read the battery directly, which is what made voltage-threshold
//   charger detection possible at the time.
//
//   Removed: the Shelly from the bike, the IRFP9140N, the 10K and the gate
//   resistor. Kept: the 1N4007, and the camera's own three wires.
//
//   Some older copies of the documentation drew the MOSFET drain going to the
//   K7's DC power input. That was never true of this installation.
//
// Device: shellyplusuni-a1b2c3d4e5f6  IP: 192.168.1.62  FW: 1.7.4
// Thing:  shelly:shellyplusuni:a1b2c3d4e5f6
// =============================================================================
Group    gMC_K7_Power               "K7 Auto-Power (box in the garage)"              <energy>               (GA_Bil)       ["PowerOutlet"]
// --- Shelly Plus Uni Channels ---
// Device: shellyplusuni-a1b2c3d4e5f6  IP: 192.168.1.62  MAC: A1B2C3D4E5F6
// MIGRATED 2026-03-26: Shelly binding broken (handleCommand never fires in 5.1.3)
// All items now virtual — updated via direct HTTP poller in JS rules.
// Relay control via HTTP to http://192.168.1.62/rpc/Switch.Set?id=0&on=true|false
Switch   MC_K7_Relay                "K7 Power Relay [MAP(k7_onoff.map):%s]"          <k7-relay-blue>        (gMC_K7_Power) ["Switch"] {autoupdate="false"}
// The ADC. It measures the voltage across the 100 Ω sense resistor in the relay
// coil's return leg — NOT a battery, despite what it measured until 2026-09-12.
// Bench-measured that day: 0.000 V with the coil unpowered or the lead out,
// 0.850-0.870 V with the coil energised (11.2 mA through 1 kΩ). The Shelly's ADC
// reads a constant 0.27 V low, confirmed at both 13 V and 1.1 V, so everything
// below 0.27 V of true voltage clamps to zero — which makes the two states
// cleaner, not worse. Battery voltage now comes from Vehicle10_Power.
Number   MC_K7_Sense_Voltage        "Coil sense [%.3f V]"                            <k7-battery-green>     (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Voltage"]
// Kept under its old name so nothing downstream silently loses its sensor during
// the migration. Retire it once every consumer has moved; see the item above.
Number   MC_K7_Shelly_Voltage       "Coil sense, legacy name [%.3f V]"               <k7-battery-green>     (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Voltage"]
// Is the garage-to-machine lead actually connected?
//
// It cannot be answered while the relay is open — with no current there is
// nothing to measure, and 0 V means "no circuit" whether the lead is in or out.
// So it is answered by ASKING: energise the coil, wait, look. See
// vehicle-motorcycle-k7-lead.js. UNDEF until the first probe, which is honest:
// unknown is not the same as disconnected.
Switch   MC_K7_Lead_Connected       "Garage lead [MAP(k7_lead.map):%s]"               <k7-relay-blue>        (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status"]
// Ask right now whether the lead is connected.
//
// It exists because the honest answer to "shouldn't I see it change when I move
// the connector?" is no: the sense resistor only carries current while the coil
// is energised, so with the relay resting open, lead in and lead out are the
// same measurement. Without this there is no way to check from the screen.
//
// Momentary: it resets itself, because a switch that stays on invites being read
// as a mode rather than a button.
Switch   MC_K7_Lead_Test            "Test lead now"                                  <k7-sync-blue>         (gMC_K7_Power) ["Switch"] {autoupdate="false"}
DateTime MC_K7_Lead_Checked         "Lead last proven [%1$td.%1$tm %1$tH:%1$tM]"     <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
// --- Shelly Device Status (HTTP-polled) ---
Number   MC_K7_Shelly_WiFi_Signal   "Shelly WiFi [%d /4]"                            <network>              (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "SignalStrength"]
Number   MC_K7_Shelly_Uptime        "Shelly Uptime [%.0f s]"                         <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Duration"]
DateTime MC_K7_Shelly_LastUpdate    "Shelly Last Update [%1$td.%1$tm %1$tH:%1$tM]"   <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
DateTime MC_K7_Shelly_Heartbeat     "Shelly Heartbeat [%1$td.%1$tm %1$tH:%1$tM]"     <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
// --- Shelly API-polled Items (updated via JS rule) ---
Number   MC_K7_Shelly_RSSI          "Shelly RSSI [%d dBm]"                           <network>              (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "RSSI"]
String   MC_K7_Shelly_SSID          "Shelly SSID [%s]"                               <network>              (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Info"]
// --- Virtual State Items (no channel binding) ---
String   MC_K7_Power_State          "K7 Power State [%s]"                            <status>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Power"]
Switch   MC_Charger_Detected        "Charger Detected [MAP(k7_onoff.map):%s]"        <k7-charger-green>     (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status"]
String   MC_K7_Power_Reason         "Power Reason [%s]"                              <text>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Power"]
DateTime MC_K7_Relay_Since          "Relay ON Since [%1$tF %1$tR]"                   <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
// --- Victron Blue Smart IP65 12/10 Charger (BLE GATT via Pi4) ---
// Pi4 daemon connects via BLE GATT 306b service, reads Victron registers,
// and posts values to openHAB REST API every 30s.
// BLE radio is active when charger has mains power. BLE Online ≠ charging:
//   Online + Idle/Off = mains power but battery cable not connected
//   Online + Bulk/Absorption/Float/Storage = actively charging
// BLE address: AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF (paired+bonded with Pi4)
Switch   MC_Charger_BLE_Online      "Charger BLE [MAP(k7_onoff.map):%s]"             <bluetooth>            (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status"]
Number   MC_Charger_BLE_RSSI        "BLE Signal [%d dBm]"                            <victron-rssi-blue-v1> (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "RSSI"]
String   MC_Charger_BLE_Signal      "BLE Signal [%s]"                                <victron-rssi-blue-v1> (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "SignalStrength"]
String   MC_Charger_Connection      "Charger [%s]"                                   <network>              (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Info"]
Number   MC_Charger_Voltage         "Charger Voltage [%.2f V]"                       <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Voltage"]
Number   MC_Charger_Current         "Charger Current [%.2f A]"                       <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Current"]
Number   MC_Charger_Current_mA      "Charger Current [%d mA]"                        <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Current"]
Number   MC_Charger_Yield           "Charged Energy [%.3f kWh]"                      <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Energy"]
String   MC_Charger_State           "Charger State [%s]"                             <heating>              (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Info"]
DateTime MC_Charger_Last_Update     "Charger Updated [%1$td.%1$tm %1$tH:%1$tM]"      <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
// --- Secondary-Connection Detection (drain prevention, added 2026-08-06) ---
// The Victron charger sits permanently on 230V mains. Its BLE "state" label
// (Storage/Float/Idle) is IDENTICAL whether the DC clamps are on the bike or
// hanging in open air — so the label alone cannot tell "connected" from
// "disconnected". 5 months of InfluxDB data proved the reliable discriminator
// is the AGREEMENT between two independent voltage sensors:
//   MC_Charger_Voltage  = Victron's own output (secondary side)
//   MC_K7_Shelly_Voltage = Shelly ADC on the actual bike battery
// Clamps ON  -> both read the same node -> delta ~0.08V (median, connected)
// Clamps OFF -> Victron floats ~13.2V open-circuit while the isolated bike
//              battery sags -> delta grows to ~0.58V (median, disconnected).
// Because the ADC offset can drift over months, we do NOT hard-code the
// delta. Instead MC_Charger_Connected_Delta LEARNS the connected baseline
// during confirmed real-current charging (>=0.3A = clamps provably on) and
// the rule flags "disconnected" only when the live delta exceeds
// baseline + tolerance. This self-calibrates and survives ADC drift.
Number   MC_Charger_Connected_Delta "Connected Baseline Δ [%.3f V]"                  <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement"]
Switch   MC_Secondary_Connected     "Secondary Connected [MAP(k7_connected.map):%s]" <k7-charger-green>     (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status"]
// Short human reason naming the proof that decided the clamp state, e.g.
// "Proof D — current seen", "Proof B — 0.35 A", "Off — no current (Proof D)".
// Set by updateChargerConnection() in vehicle-motorcycle-k7-power.js.
String   MC_Secondary_Reason        "Clamp Detection [%s]"                           <text>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Info"]
// --- Proof D: Secondary-Connection via BLE Data Richness (added 2026-08-09) ---
// The charger exposes NO 'secondary connected' register (Victron-confirmed;
// 0xEDD5/0xEDD7 proved to be plain mirrors in a live clamp on/off A/B test).
// But the BLE STREAM changes with the clamp state: when the clamps are on the
// bike, charge-current registers appear in the cycle (current can only flow in
// a closed circuit). MC_Charger_Secondary_Proof is the daemon's verdict
// ("Connected (current seen)" / "Off? ..." / "Uncertain ...") and IS now the
// PRIMARY input to isSecondaryConnected() in the JS rule.
// Reg_Count/Data_Bytes were the A/B-test raw evidence — proven unreliable as
// discriminators (both states overlap), so they are kept for InfluxDB history
// only and are no longer shown on the sitemap.
Number   MC_Charger_Reg_Count       "BLE Registers/Cycle [%d]"                       <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement"]
Number   MC_Charger_Data_Bytes      "BLE Data/Cycle [%d B]"                          <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement"]
String   MC_Charger_Secondary_Proof "Proof D (Clamps) [%s]"                          <network>              (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Info"]
// The prick (2026-10-14): when Proof D falls to Off?/Uncertain the daemon switches the
// charge preset Normal -> High -> Normal (register 0xEDF1), which restarts the cycle; a
// battery on the clamps then takes current even when full. Automatic at most every 12 h;
// MC_Charger_Prick ON = prick on the next cycle (the daemon switches it back OFF).
// victron-ble/README.md "Writing: the charge preset restarts the cycle".
Switch   MC_Charger_Prick           "Probe charger now"                              <victron-charger-blue> (gMC_K7_Power) ["Control"]
String   MC_Charger_Prick_Result    "Last charger probe [%s]"                        <victron-state-teal>   (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Info"]
// --- Charge Session History (persisted to InfluxDB) ---
// Updated by vehicle-motorcycle-k7-charge-history.js on each charge cycle.
DateTime MC_Charge_Session_Start    "Session Start [%1$td.%1$tm %1$tH:%1$tM]"        <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
DateTime MC_Charge_Session_End      "Session End [%1$td.%1$tm %1$tH:%1$tM]"          <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Timestamp"]
Number   MC_Charge_Session_Minutes  "Session Duration [%.0f min]"                    <clock-schedule-blue>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement"]
Number   MC_Charge_Session_V_Start  "Start Voltage [%.2f V]"                         <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Voltage"]
Number   MC_Charge_Session_V_End    "End Voltage [%.2f V]"                           <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Voltage"]
Number   MC_Charge_Session_V_Delta  "Voltage Change [%.2f V]"                        <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Voltage"]
Number   MC_Charge_Session_Wh       "Energy Charged [%.1f Wh]"                       <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement", "Energy"]
String   MC_Charge_Session_Peak     "Peak Stage [%s]"                                <energy>               (gMC_K7_Power) ["Status", "Power"]
Number   MC_Charge_Session_Count    "Total Sessions [%.0f]"                          <none>                 (gMC_K7_Power) ["Measurement"]
